        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_24aef2ed7f184479858914008c6d59f3",
      "statement": "Under the active_facts convention readers never see facts of unfinished runs: the extraction-agent writes one artifact version's element set in a single transaction (re-extraction replaces the set, dropping HAS_ELEMENT edges for un reproduced elements); the tlr-agent writes links inactive in batches and activates them in the run's final transaction, which also deactivates earlier links of the same approach between the same versions; the inconsistency-agent writes one detection run in one transaction; consequently readers never need Run.status.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://adr/0005-kg-schema-provenance-versioning.md#L89-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d30a6aeeaac909e02312c8d2c9522faaa356d61f8539877ef15cd26b80f138cb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://contracts/kg/schema.yaml#L10-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79acea318e766e22c9aeb8e6755375fdd52ac4e56548f23e3e9f0158d59f1f7b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a7a17f122ca5493eb2ea612d20b86dfd",
      "statement": "Ids are deterministic stableIds (prefix_hex32) over their arguments (e.g. tl_ = stableId(approach, approachVersion, configHash, sourceId, targetId), inc_ = stableId(projectId, fingerprint)), making re-runs idempotent; only Run ids are random (run_hex32).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://adr/0005-kg-schema-provenance-versioning.md#L29-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:29019707315ecb7b332426483222ba9beeda29c7ecd315a30329ac237cb50ea1:"
